        <h1>Privacy Policy — BillCheck PK</h1>
        <p>This privacy policy applies to the <strong>BillCheck PK</strong> mobile application (hereby referred to as "Application", "App", or "Service") for Android mobile devices, created and maintained by <strong>Digi Tools</strong> (hereby referred to as "Service Provider", "we", "us", or "our") as a free service with optional premium subscription enhancements. This Service is provided "AS IS".</p>

        <div class="disclaimer-box">
            <p><strong>IMPORTANT NON-AFFILIATION NOTICE:</strong> BillCheck PK is an independent third-party utility tracker. We are <strong>NOT affiliated with, endorsed by, sponsored by, or connected to the Government of Pakistan, NEPRA, OGRA, PTA, WAPDA, or any utility provider</strong> (e.g., LESCO, MEPCO, SNGPL, WASA, PTCL). The Application acts strictly as a web viewer/parser accessing publicly available online utility billing portals for personal consumer tracking.</p>
        </div>

        <h2>1. Information Collection and Storage</h2>
        <p>The Application collects and processes information entered by you as well as diagnostic telemetry necessary to deliver utility bill tracking services.</p>

        <h3>A. Utility Account & Billing Information</h3>
        <p>To check, organize, and monitor your monthly bills, you may input utility account identifiers:</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Consumer Numbers, Reference Numbers, Account IDs, and Meter Identifiers:</strong> Used strictly to fetch current and historical bill details from your respective utility provider's public web server.</li>
            <li><strong>Retrieved Bill Data:</strong> Customer billing name, payable amount, due date, billing month, units consumed, tariff category, and raw bill slips.</li>
        </ul>

        <div class="alert-box">
            <p><strong>ON-DEVICE LOCAL STORAGE (ROOM DATABASE):</strong> All your entered reference numbers, account nicknames, and downloaded bill slips are stored <strong>LOCALLY on your device</strong> in a sandboxed, encrypted SQLite database (`Room`). This allows you to view and review your bills completely offline. You retain total control: deleting any bill from your history immediately and permanently purges it from your device.</p>
        </div>

        <h3>B. Optional Cloud Backup & Account Data (Google Sign-In)</h3>
        <p>Unlike basic offline-only apps, BillCheck PK offers an <em>optional</em> cloud backup feature. If you choose to sign in with your Google account:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>We collect your basic public profile information: Google Display Name, Email Address, Profile Picture URL, and unique Firebase User Identifier (`UID`).</li>
            <li>Your saved bill reference numbers and basic summary metadata are synchronized with Google Cloud Firestore (`users/{uid}/bills`) to allow seamless multi-device restoration.</li>
            <li>Full HTML bill copies remain stored exclusively on your device storage.</li>
            <li><strong>Complete Data Deletion:</strong> You can permanently wipe your cloud backup and profile at any time directly within the app under <strong>Settings → Account → Delete Cloud Account & Data</strong>.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>C. Automatically Collected Device & Technical Data</h3>
        <p>When you use the Application, certain telemetry is automatically collected:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Your device's Internet Protocol (IP) address (used solely for coarse regional localization and security).</li>
            <li>Device hardware model, operating system version, carrier, and screen dimensions.</li>
            <li>Application interaction telemetry (timestamps, visited screens, session duration).</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>2. Device Permissions Requested</h2>
        <p>To provide its core utility viewing functions, the Application requires the following standard Android permissions:</p>
        <table class="badge-table">
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th>Permission</th>
                    <th>Technical Identifier</th>
                    <th>Purpose</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr>
                    <td><strong>Internet Access</strong></td>
                    <td><code>android.permission.INTERNET</code></td>
                    <td>To fetch publicly available bill slips from utility provider web portals and sync cloud backups.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><strong>Network State</strong></td>
                    <td><code>android.permission.ACCESS_NETWORK_STATE</code></td>
                    <td>To check active connectivity before querying utility portals, avoiding unnecessary data usage.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><strong>Bill Notifications</strong></td>
                    <td><code>android.permission.POST_NOTIFICATIONS</code></td>
                    <td>Required on Android 13+ to deliver local bill due-date reminder alerts prior to payment deadlines.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><strong>Storage (Legacy)</strong></td>
                    <td><code>android.permission.WRITE_EXTERNAL_STORAGE</code></td>
                    <td>Used exclusively on Android 9 (API 28) and older when you explicitly choose to export or save a bill slip image or PDF.</td>
                </tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>

        <h2>3. Third-Party Service Providers & Advertising</h2>
        <p>Only aggregated, anonymized data is periodically transmitted to external services to aid the Service Provider in optimizing performance, maintaining security, and supporting free access.</p>

        <h3>A. Advertising Networks (`adsModule`)</h3>
        <p>For users on the free tier, third-party advertisements are displayed. These networks may process your Google Advertising ID (GAID), IP address, and ad interaction events:</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Google AdMob:</strong> <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Privacy & Terms</a></li>
            <li><strong>Meta Audience Network (Facebook Ads):</strong> <a href="https://www.facebook.com/about/privacy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Meta Privacy Policy</a></li>
            <li><strong>Google User Messaging Platform (UMP):</strong> Delivers European (GDPR/ePrivacy) consent choices, allowing users to customize tracking preferences.</li>
        </ul>
        <p><em>Users who upgrade to the Pro Plan enjoy a completely ad-free experience with third-party advertising modules disabled.</em></p>

        <h3>B. Analytics, Crash Reporting & Quality</h3>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Google Play Services & Firebase Analytics:</strong> Aggregated user journey tracking.</li>
            <li><strong>Firebase Crashlytics:</strong> Automated capture of crash stack traces and device states to quickly resolve bugs.</li>
            <li><strong>Firebase Remote Config:</strong> Dynamic app configuration management.</li>
            <li><strong>UXCam:</strong> Diagnostic session replay and heatmap analysis to identify UI friction and navigational errors. UXCam does not record sensitive payment fields.</li>
            <li><strong>PostHog:</strong> In-app product analytics and feature engagement.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>C. Subscriptions & In-App Purchases</h3>
        <p>In-app subscriptions (Standard Monthly, Pro Monthly) are managed through <strong>Google Play Billing</strong> and <strong>RevenueCat</strong>. We <strong>never collect, process, or store credit card numbers or banking information</strong>. Google Play processes all transactions in accordance with Google's secure financial standards.</p>

        <h2>4. Background Due-Date Reminders (WorkManager)</h2>
        <p>The Application includes an automated bill alert scheduler using Android WorkManager. This background task runs <strong>100% locally on your smartphone</strong>, comparing your device calendar clock against saved bill due dates to alert you before surcharges apply. No bill data is uploaded to external servers for this feature.</p>

        <h2>5. Information Disclosure Policy</h2>
        <p>The Service Provider may disclose User Provided and Automatically Collected Information only under the following limited circumstances:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>As required by law, such as to comply with a valid court subpoena or legal process;</li>
            <li>When we believe in good faith that disclosure is necessary to protect our legal rights, ensure personal safety, investigate fraud, or comply with government requests;</li>
            <li>With trusted infrastructure service providers (e.g., Google Firebase) who work on our behalf and have agreed to adhere strictly to this privacy policy.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>6. Opt-Out & Data Deletion Rights</h2>
        <p>You have full autonomy over your data:</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Local Data:</strong> You can remove individual bills or clear your entire history in the app. Uninstalling the app permanently purges all local Room database entries.</li>
            <li><strong>Cloud Data:</strong> Navigate to <strong>Settings → Account → Delete Cloud Account & Data</strong> to permanently wipe your cloud backup and Google profile association.</li>
            <li><strong>Email Request:</strong> You may also request deletion by contacting us at <a href="mailto:digitools.it@gmail.com">digitools.it@gmail.com</a>.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>7. Children's Privacy</h2>
        <p>The Application does not knowingly solicit data from or market to children under the age of 13. If the Service Provider discovers that personal information has been provided by a child under 13, it will be deleted immediately. Parents or guardians may contact us at <a href="mailto:digitools.it@gmail.com">digitools.it@gmail.com</a> to request immediate action.</p>

        <h2>8. Security Safeguards</h2>
        <p>The Service Provider provides commercial-grade physical, electronic, and procedural safeguards to protect the confidentiality of your data, including HTTPS/TLS network encryption and sandboxed local application storage.</p>

